{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce","id":1481875,"title":"The Salubri who are known as the good guys, regularly consorted with the Tzimisce","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-24T16:10:21-07:00","id":1481875,"title":"The Salubri who are known as the good guys, regularly consorted with the Tzimisce","content":"In the dark ages salubri clanbook, we learn that the salubri and tzimisce have a very close relationship. In fact it is stated that warriors and healers of clan salubri were able to learn more about their powers by watching the tzimisce torture their victims. So why is it that a clan that's supposed to be filled with paragons of justice are willing to consort with such sadistic monsters?<br /> <br /> It becomes kind of funny when you realize that they talk bad about almost every other clan, but one of the clans they seem to have only good things to say about are the tzimisce. Looking at this, its easy to see why the other clans were willing to turn their backs on the salubri, you cant preach justice and at the same time hangout with tyrants that enjoy torturing their subjects.<br /> <br /> -You can find it in Salubri Dark ages clanbook page 35","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":".  Putting the location of the information 05-25-2022, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T16:24:32-07:00","id":1481876,"title":"","content":"I believe the Healers consorted with both Tzimisce and Cappadocians, but the Warriors are rumored to have encountered the Eldest and actually attacked him (as per one of the rumors from the Tzimisce Revised clanbook). I do understand what you are getting at in regards to their weird alliance and I never quite understood it myself, but maybe the Salubri were always less human than some of the writeups had you believe.<br /> <br /> I think that had no real impact on why the other clans let them implode under Tremere pressure, though. I think it was just expedient to get rid of the moralistic Salubri in exchange of Tremere Thaumaturgy and boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":11263,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","user":"Gimmisky","date":". 05-25-2022, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T16:27:00-07:00","id":1481877,"title":"","content":"Best guess? Both Tzim and Saulot are deeply concerned about enlightenment, and didn't really care much about how it was achieved. Saulot eventually settled on seeking Golconda and Tzim eventually settled on achieving Metamorphosis, but for a very long time they were both just a couple of scholar/mystics who compared notes and had a pretty good relationship as Antes go. This friendship trickled down to their clans and resulted in a lot of odd couples for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T16:41:20-07:00","id":1481879,"title":"","content":"This is mostly an artifact that there isn't really canonical continuity between the versions of the World of Darkness after 30 years (or even 10). There's at least 3, maybe 5 or even more &quot;worlds&quot; out there that are similar, but not identical like the old Earth-1, Earth-2, Earth-3, etc. of DC comics. There's enough changes between the Vampire: the Dark Ages setting and the implied backstory of 1e/2e Vampire that the two aren't actually compatible if you look close enough at the details. Different developers had their own ideas and goals, they weren't necessarily interested in keeping with the original ideas of the game's founders.<br /> <br /> However, how good the Salubri were is always something to question. Even when first introduced as a tiny seven member bloodline, there were enough bizarre customs and actions about the Salubri that made a lot of people scratch their heads. And while the Salubri as &quot;good guys&quot; is something of an OOC take because of their quest for Golconda and caregiver natures, IC their reputation was mostly BAD. And the idea that there were two kinds of Salubri - the original kind, and then the second kind after Saulot had supposedly found Golconda - always left some ambiguity (In essence, I see them as two different clans albeit with the same founder).<br /> <br /> I've always had ambivalent feelings about the Dark Ages Salubri clanbook. While there's some parts that I like, I didn't like the presentation as a whole. It didn't present the Salubri in a way I felt they should have been portrayed before they reduced to the strange bloodline that existed in the Modern Day. But I felt that about most of the Dark Ages line, and it got only worse when V:tDA became DA:V. But obviously those sourcebooks have lots of fans, and their canon is held to whatever WoD-5 version that exists today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T17:26:14-07:00","id":1481880,"title":"","content":"The Salubri can be considered &quot;good guys&quot; as far as vampires go. But they're still vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T18:14:31-07:00","id":1481884,"title":"","content":"Saulot specifically was a &quot;the ends justifies the means&quot; kind of person. If he was put into the trolly problem, he would shove the fat guy onto the tracks without hesitation. That said, Saulot does have a moral compass. He'll do things that save the most people if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Grammar 05-25-2022, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T18:24:22-07:00","id":1481886,"title":"","content":"I kind of picture Saulot and Tzim as old friends, one of which has gone vegan, and the other of which loves bacon so much she posts bacon memes on social media. From the pigs' perspective they should be worst enemies. But from their perspective? The bacon lover still enjoys having her friend over, even if she'd like her to shut up about how much better she feels since she went vegan. They kind of sigh and roll their eyes at each other periodically, but they are still friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T22:57:28-07:00","id":1481898,"title":"","content":"The Salubri, both the Helaers and Warriors were always pragmatist.<br /> Like CajunKhan said, nohing prevent them to be friends and respect the other. Not to mention, when you are a guest somewhere (and hospitality was/is important to the Tzimisce) you keep your mouth shout about the taste of your host to not to offend him. But on the other hand I think a Tzimisce host tonned back a little with the experiments and torture when a Salubri guest was around, not to upset or make them uncomfortable.<br /> A Salubri could have visited a Tzimisce for any number of reasons, maybe they wanted to train with the fearsome slachta, or seek counsel about spirits and demons, or just even to ease the pain of the humans on the domain of a Tzimisce. From the Tzimsice perspective, torture and experiments never were made becasue hurr durr im eeebil(tm), they have a reason for it. Scientific reason, social reason, but a reason. Their &quot;justice&quot; was harsh, but the Salubri I guess never questioned why their host punish his mortals such harshly, they just nodded, well, if you say so that poor soul deserved it... oooh so thats an artery!<br /> The Tzimsice were perfectly fine with their &quot;warhound&quot; Gangrel guests roaming their domain or let the swamp or caves the home of a Nosferatu, and actually they never treated those &quot;low clans&quot; worse than anyone else; in the Tzimsice eyes, everyone in the world are equal... equally under THEM, no need to treat them differently. And the Salubri actually had much to learn from them, in turn kept their herd/domain healthy or helped to hunt down a Kupala or two, or pesky shadow Lord that wandered in, shaking his fist &quot;muh honor, you killed my father, my father's father, my father's father's father....!!!&quot; Don't mind the puppy dear guest, I'm an old associate of the family...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-25-2022, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T23:13:00-07:00","id":1481899,"title":"","content":"Do we really need <i>another </i>thread that points out a flaw in the lore? Assuming there actually is one and it's not just cherry-picked details designed to provoke a reaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T23:58:21-07:00","id":1481901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481899#post1481899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we really need <i>another </i>thread that points out a flaw in the lore? Assuming there actually is one and it's not just cherry-picked details designed to provoke a reaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Provocative hot takes are the OP's whole thing, though. I don't mean that as a criticism, necessarily, I think these threads can be entertaining if approached with the right mindset.<br /> <br /> As for the main topic, my thoughts and preferences are once again closely aligned with those of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>. From the beginning, the Salubri have been presented as a group with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450257-children-of-osiris?p=1455479#post1455479\">very strange beliefs and practices</a>. The popular conception among White Wolf fandom that the Salubri are nothing but a designated good guy group does not survive close examination. This does not mean that they should be presented as an equally simplistic asshole group, either, only that the Salubri have always (in terms of publication history, not ingame lore) exhibited cultish or otherwise questionable behavior. It's one reason why I always quite enjoyed the <i>Dark Ages</i> idea of mutual respect between the Salubri and the Tzimisce... Even if it is another example of later White Wolf writers treating vampires as clan members first and individuals second. In the Dark Medieval setting, clan association should mean even less than it does in modern nights because of how scattered and disorganized Cainite society is during the Long Night, but that's not where the <i>Dark Ages</i> developers took the game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T00:18:30-07:00","id":1481902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481880#post1481880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Salubri can be considered &quot;good guys&quot; as far as vampires go. But they're still vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also feel like trying to make the Tzimisce &quot;bad&quot; vampires is a bit ridiculous.<br /> <br /> They're all bad vampires.<br /> <br /> Pre-Sabbat, the Tzimisce were not that much worse than anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T07:58:50-07:00","id":1481922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481902#post1481902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also feel like trying to make the Tzimisce &quot;bad&quot; vampires is a bit ridiculous.<br /> <br /> They're all bad vampires.<br /> <br /> Pre-Sabbat, the Tzimisce were not that much worse than anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IDK about that. Reading through their clanbook, it seems like their favourite pastime in the dark ages was wiping out villages and torturing individuals. I remember reading up back stories of characters who had their whole village wiped out at the whim of their tzimisce overlords. No other clan has done that. When most vampire have sadistic tendencies, its really the vampire in question that's depraved, not the entire clan. But it feels like the tzimisce as a whole have a clan culture of torture and other depraved acts and they seem to pass down this habit to their descendants as well.<br /> <br /> Although I do agree with you that almost all vampires tend to be bad, its just that some are worse than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-25-2022, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T09:53:28-07:00","id":1481931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481899#post1481899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we really need <i>another </i>thread that points out a flaw in the lore? Assuming there actually is one and it's not just cherry-picked details designed to provoke a reaction?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Don't thread bomb.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T11:23:44-07:00","id":1481940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481877#post1481877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Best guess? Both Tzim and Saulot are deeply concerned about enlightenment, and didn't really care much about how it was achieved. Saulot eventually settled on seeking Golconda and Tzim eventually settled on achieving Metamorphosis, but for a very long time they were both just a couple of scholar/mystics who compared notes and had a pretty good relationship as Antes go.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an important point. The legends surrounding both Antes depict them searching for avenues to transcend the curse of the vampire, and it's possible that the word &quot;enlightenment&quot; gets tossed around only for want of a more precise term or understanding on the part of the tellers.<br /> <br /> Something happens to the Salubri's reputation after the diablerie of Saulot. Elders of other clans look back on him as a martyr (now that he's considered safely dead) while going along with the painting of his childer as filthy demoniacs, and there's a bit of having it both ways here. The High Clans definitely want to stay on the good side of these Tremere usurpers, who have proven themselves a force to be reckoned with, but they certainly want to discourage a repeat of the diablerie within their own clans. <br /> <br /> We're not left with a truly objective source on who Saulot was, at all. If he was truly the founder of the Baali, at what point did he fall? Had he started exploring his own inner darkness when he egged on Tzimisce's inhumanity, the way Moloch is said to have done to Troile in some tellings of the fall of Carthage? Sure, maybe. Why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T12:13:34-07:00","id":1481944,"title":"","content":"Always think it\u2019s a black humor which is everywhere within WoD\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T12:14:14-07:00","id":1481945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce#post1481875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the dark ages salubri clanbook, we learn that the salubri and tzimisce have a very close relationship. In fact it is stated that warriors and healers of clan salubri were able to learn more about their powers by watching the tzimisce torture their victims. So why is it that a clan that's supposed to be filled with paragons of justice are willing to consort with such sadistic monsters?<br /> <br /> It becomes kind of funny when you realize that they talk bad about almost every other clan, but one of the clans they seem to have only good things to say about are the tzimisce. Looking at this, its easy to see why the other clans were willing to turn their backs on the salubri, you cant preach justice and at the same time hangout with tyrants that enjoy torturing their subjects.<br /> <br /> -You can find it in Salubri Dark ages clanbook page 35</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you intentionally exaggerating for effect on this &quot;they talk bad about almost every other clan&quot; thing? I ask because in the clanbook you're talking about, the Healer Salubri providing perspective feels they legitimately wronged the Assamites as a clan in supporting the Crusades and regrets being unable to find forgiveness from them, the Warrior Salubri respects them as warriors and notes having been happy to leave a battlefield without killing one, and the third person objective narrative notes that the Salubri look at their former stance overall with embarrassment. They regard the Brujah as friends. A healer Salubri sacrificed their lives to save a Gangrel from being made into a Gargoyle, with several other Gangrel coming forward to note having received similar defense and the Salubri are noted as regarding the clan overall with respect. They speak of the Malkavians and Nosferatu well.<br /> <br /> That's.. *counts* five clans. Of the remaining 8ish, their main note on the Ravnos is being confused by them, they're obviously not going to like the Tremere, nor the clans actively handing them over to the Tremere, nor the Setites and the Baali. It otherwise notes that before the Ventrue started going &quot;nah, kill em, that's fine&quot;, they had a positive opinion of the Ventrue that was let down by the whole &quot;nah, kill em, that's fine&quot; thing. Why would they not &quot;talk bad&quot; about clans actively engaged in making them dead? (You can score some points for inconsistency off their take on the Cappadocians I suppose, if that's mostly what this whole thing was an effort to do).<br /> <br /> It's less &quot;kind of funny&quot; and more, you seem to be leaving a lot of context out and exaggerating some content over others. Yeah, they have a close relationship with the Tzimisce. Yeah, it's not great. It's as though all clans are flawed, even ones ostensibly trying to strive for some measure of decency. And that the book presented things as being more complicated than &quot;they had it coming for the Tzimisce thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> But otherwise<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It becomes kind of funny when you realize that they talk bad about almost every other clan </div> </div> </div>Their opinions on other clans and the context these opinions exist in are more nuanced than you seem to be willing to acknowledge.<br /> <br /> I get that twitter style &quot;thank you for coming to my TED talk&quot; provoke people hot take posts are fun, I guess? Like trying to be that &quot;debate me!&quot; meme guy or something? But the game at least tries for some nuance when presenting things. This instead has a pretty solid Matt Bors &quot;We Should Improve Society Somewhat&quot; comics vibe honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-25-2022, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T13:47:12-07:00","id":1481949,"title":"","content":"The salubri Definitely have some clashing lore. From the outside, It looks like some writers wanted to make a clan that wasn't weighed down by all the &quot;and they were secretly evil because X&quot; that was prolific in the other clans, while others didn't want a &quot;designated good guy&quot; clan.<br /> <br /> This gets even more muddled with the era between 2nd and revised where some of the writers decided Saulot should be a BBEG trying to become the demon emperor(despite that being a wan kuei issue and having nothing to do with the eurasian + african territories that cainites were based in) and responsible for everything bad ever starting with the diablerie of his own clan up to possibly the creation of the Baali(can we also talk about the fact that this would mean Saulot effectively invented 4 disciplines? Making him second only to Caine, who created 8[not including blood magic], in discipline creation).<br /> <br /> The salubri are locus of retcons and their lore is definitely muddled for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T16:27:15-07:00","id":1481957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481945#post1481945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>Who is this Mat Bors you speak of?<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't you find it funny when someone preaches justice and scolds others for the actions they commit, just to ignore their friend who is committing far more heinous crimes?<br /> <br /> The salubri healer, stated that they ignored the acts of torture that was being committed by their tzimisce hosts. There is no nuance to this, they purposely chose to ignore the evil that was happening around them because it was convenient for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 05-25-2022, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T16:47:57-07:00","id":1481959,"title":"","content":"He's the author or this comic strip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thenib.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mister-gotcha-1-8387eb-1.featfeatured.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/\" target=\"_blank\"> Mister Gotcha | The Nib </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Calling out all hypocrisy all the way. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think the comparison is fair or accurate, unless I've seriously misread you. Bors is zinging a type of person who tries to shut conversation off in service to the status quo, while you're the most active conversation starter on the board right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T17:07:05-07:00","id":1481961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481959#post1481959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's the author or this comic strip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thenib.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/mister-gotcha-1-8387eb-1.featfeatured.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/\" target=\"_blank\"> Mister Gotcha | The Nib </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://thenib.com/mister-gotcha/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Calling out all hypocrisy all the way. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think the comparison is fair or accurate, unless I've seriously misread you. Bors is zinging a type of person who tries to shut conversation off in service to the status quo, while you're the most active conversation starter on the board right now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! I'm not too knowledgeable on these types of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T17:31:11-07:00","id":1481965,"title":"","content":"I just remembered a fact thanks to the wiki. Saulot most likely sired the Baali founders. Granted there's a theory just about every clan being the original baali sires, but Saulot has an interesting theme to it.<br /> <br /> First, Saulot and the warriors were the most active in the Baali wars, and were even more determined to finish off the Baali then the Banu Haqim! In addition, some say the Baali founders came from the east, and Saulot did journey to and from the east in search of knowledge.<br /> <br /> So here's my theory. Saulot sired the baali founders, maybe out of petty or for a greater purpose. After the baali became a serious threat to the world, Saulot then decided they needed to be purged. Again, Saulot isn't perfect. He does do what he thinks will help the most people, but he makes a lot of mistakes. Like possibly sireing the kindred's most infamous bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T18:58:58-07:00","id":1481968,"title":"","content":"The Saulot as Baali founder thing primarily comes from two sources: an unreliable narrator in a Dark Ages clanbook, and a pair of quite possibly forged documents in the Transylvania Chronicle series of adventures for Dark Ages. Assuming it's true, it's not inconceivable that the war could have been an acid test to see which of Saulot's toys was the most durable. <br /> <br /> As always when we're talking about events that took place that long ago, the uncertainty is deliberate. I happen to like that theory, but it could just as easily be propaganda planted by the Tremere, the Baali, or somebody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-25-2022, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T19:19:02-07:00","id":1481969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481957#post1481957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who is this Mat Bors you speak of?<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't you find it funny when someone preaches justice and scolds others for the actions they commit, just to ignore their friend who is committing far more heinous crimes?<br /> <br /> The salubri healer, stated that they ignored the acts of torture that was being committed by their tzimisce hosts. There is no nuance to this, they purposely chose to ignore the evil that was happening around them because it was convenient for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And other Salubri gave their lives to stop Gangrel from being killed and mutilated in Tremere experiments enough times that multiple Gangrel noted that being a thing. And other Salubri fell so hard into a desperate need for vengeance that they intentionally lost whatever scrap of grace they might have had just for a chance to sate their rage. And other Salubri reached Golconda. And other Salubri became willing, even knowing pawns of the twisted schemes of a Fallen Saulot. And other Salubri saved various and sundry mortals from being killed even at the risk of their own lives, or loss of their own lives. That's all in the clanbook.<br /> <br /> The Salubri having ideals that sometimes they live by, and sometimes they die for the sake of, and sometimes they fail, and sometimes they're big ol hypocrites about is a portrayal with decent enough depth for me as far as their clanbook went. It helps them not feel like a monolith or stereotype as opposed to a fleshed out thing. That this one part of it is something you're hyperfocused on is.. sure? It certainly seems more important to you than anything else in the book such that when that stuff is brought up, you just keep repeating this one thing.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't really change that your whole &quot;talk bad about almost every other clan&quot; requires ignoring they speak positively or at least regretfully about a bunch of clans, and the context of the statements on several of the clans they do speak badly about.<br /> <br /> It's also pretty true to life that people will rationalize and accept all sorts of awful things when their lives are at stake, or even just when they can get something out of it. The healer notes he disagrees with what his host is doing, but we see he's ultimately decided survival is more important than his ideals, as did a variety of the Salubri who tried to shelter with the clan. The clanbook notes some not to fleeing to the East at all and instead stick to their principles/focusing on fighting the infernal/continuing to tend to people about them/trying to hide within their existing communities/etc. On the other hand, we as readers know they are going to die for that choice (and also most of the ones in the East later on, but that's not especially tragic). But Vampire tends to make grim statements like that about what ideology and cleaving to it can get you.<br /> <br /> It's funny if you want to act like it's the only thing in there, I guess? For me it makes them more real. Beliefs get compromised, beliefs get followed imperfectly, or even badly. People who strive for virtue are very often the most blind to their own failures of living by that virtue. Even and especially glaring failures.<br /> <br /> And yet, just sometimes, some of such people actually manage to pull off living by their ideals to a way that can make them seem worthwhile. Even dying by them for the sake of another.<br /> <br /> Both these concepts are in the clanbook, and it's better for it that they both are, for my own experience. Your own reaction is apparently vastly different. Which again, sure. But also again, when you say stuff like &quot;they talk bad about almost every other clan&quot;, and talk about the clan being big ol scolds, and etc. etc. that's all the same a fairly disingenuous take as far as the actual book content. It feels somewhat less like you want some discussion on these things and more want a chorus about how dumb and laughable and evil the Salubri and their presentation are. You've not especially replied to anything I brought up and instead just keep repeating the thing about the Tzimisce. It makes it a bit difficult to feel like the idea is to constructively discuss any of this and more to go &quot;gotcha, the Salubri and anyone into them!&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean we could also go beyond the clanbook to places where various Salubri had a far more negative view of the Tzimisce at the time, or that some of those who took shelter with them tried to make sure they did it with such handful of non grotesque Tzim as there might be, but it doesn't really feel like you want to discuss that, given the state of replies to others bringing up &quot;well there's a lot of inconsistent setting writing on the Salubri&quot;. Which, there definitely is. So, clanbook it is I guess?<br /> <br /> Also while we're there the idea that the DA Tzimisce were especially worse than the other clans doesn't really bear out in the overall setting material, or even one of the overarching themes of the Dark Ages era across several lines. They all have terrible crap they've been party to. The Ventrue alone committed some breathtaking atrocities during their wars with them in the Dark Ages period. The entire Shadow Reconquista was in many ways pretty unpleasant as multi clan wars go. Vicissitude just let the Tzim be more gross about what they do comparatively. This is otherwise the era where roads like the Road of Sin are major roads with significant multiclan devotion. The coarse, very often cruel unsubtlety with which vampires as an overall whole generally treated humanity is part of what ultimately leads to the Burning Times.<br /> <br /> You seem to want to have some kind of statement of definitive absolutes here. I don't really feel like it bears out. Otherwise I guess I'd say something like &quot;do you think the various Gangrel for whom various Salubri died then went 'yeaaah, but the Tzimisce tho!'&quot; and act like one cancels out the other. Because they don't. They're just both things that are there. The book at least seems to want to try to say that while the Salubri had faults, some of them regardless kept true to a set of better ideals, and it's kinda sad that is part of what got them killed. I feel like it did a pretty solid job of that.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting, I say &quot;objective third person narration&quot; at one point, but that itself isn't accurate on my part especially. Except for the rules writing and sample pc writeups, the entire book is always from some character's perspective, the narrator is himself another vampire. People tend to miss that about these things and thus leap to a definitive take on things when it's all.. not that. This was a problem with a lot of material from this era of White Wolf and fan reaction to it. From Changeling to Vampire, a lot of stuff got written in character, not out of character, and thereby marrying to a view of it as final, it has, you know, problems. Hence some of my qualifiers like &quot;the book at least seems to want to try to say...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":".  noticed a grammar thing 05-26-2022, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T19:55:12-07:00","id":1481972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481968#post1481968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Saulot as Baali founder thing primarily comes from two sources: an unreliable narrator in a Dark Ages clanbook, and a pair of quite possibly forged documents in the Transylvania Chronicle series of adventures for Dark Ages. Assuming it's true, it's not inconceivable that the war could have been an acid test to see which of Saulot's toys was the most durable.<br /> <br /> As always when we're talking about events that took place that long ago, the uncertainty is deliberate. I happen to like that theory, but it could just as easily be propaganda planted by the Tremere, the Baali, or somebody else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I'm talking about when the narrator is objective third person or not, we do get objective third person narration in places in the revised era going &quot;Saulot, he was once good, but then became super the worst evil and you're all one microscopic cog in his catastrophic plan.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was true until it itself took something of a retcon (around the end of Revised, Lair of the Hidden has him just &quot;switch back to being good&quot;, more or less, while acknowledging he had before that been doing a pile of evil crap, and V20 tried to square the circle of the entire mess by implying there's a Good Saulot, and an Evil Saulot both running around).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 05-25-2022, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T20:04:06-07:00","id":1481973,"title":"","content":"Evil Saulot noticeably does not appear in *any* of the scenarios from the old Gehenna book, to my supreme disappointment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T20:11:16-07:00","id":1481974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481973#post1481973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evil Saulot noticeably does not appear in *any* of the scenarios from the old Gehenna book, to my supreme disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gehenna went off Lair of the Hidden, itself a Time of Judgement book that came out a few months before it, where Saulot is acknowledged as having once been Evil Saulot, but is now instead Tarnished Good Saulot. So for Gehenna purposes, he's that.<br /> <br /> It was personally unsatisfying and felt arbitrary. &quot;Why is he good again now? Because reasons.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get that any number of people did not like that Saulot was changed into Evil Saulot for Revised, but if you're going to change him back, and right near the end of the gameline, at least parse it out better, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T21:27:30-07:00","id":1481982,"title":"","content":"Oh, while I'm there, since this thread is otherwise on the idea of the Tzimisce of the Dark Ages being one of the worst clans of the time or what have you, it seems on point to note that this is the era where canonically vampires across a variety of of clans, skewing heavily Toreador and Ventrue, outright gleefully took part in and otherwise supported and encouraged the Albigensian Crusade. A war a variety of historians regard as one of Medieval Europe's in territory genocides.<br /> <br /> The Dark Ages Tzimisce's deeds are certainly more viscerally attention grabbing, but they didn't really corner the market, to put it one way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T22:11:57-07:00","id":1481983,"title":"","content":"Beckett's Jyhad Diary tied that Evil and Good Saulot thing up nicely, with Saulot P'o running amok and became the White Worm under Vienna while his Hun manifested as the &quot;Good Saulot&quot;<br /> This based on the tie with Kuei Jin, Saulot as Zao-Lat, a student of Xue, a thief, a despicable creature who benefited from Xue's compassion, learned Ch'iuh Muh - wich he not really udnerstanded and refined to be Valeren - then ran back home leaving behind his mess the Wu Zao and along the way made a Baali, when his P'o took control - or you know very Devil Tiger like behavior; the formation of the Baali may have been, in some incomprehensible way, a service for good in the long run. Clanbook: Baali suggests the Baali's ultimate purpose is the setting of chthonic entities (called Children) with sacrifice. Without these sacrifices, the Children would awaken and devour creation. Thus, the Baali's seeming evil protects humanity from a worse fate. Saulot may have sired the Baali to serve this purpose.<br /> More so, Kindred of the East allows you as a salubri player to actually awaken your P'o (beast) and start your Dharmic journey (players guide I think)!<br /> Then again, in V20 Goratrix during the Dark Ages was, in fact, Tremere, having been forced outside his body after he was possessed by Saulot<br /> Wich actually lines up nicely in Lair o the Hidden where Mokur (the Jomon potter golconda teacher from Japan) when was &quot;captured&quot; asked his captors to &quot;take him to his Father&quot;<br /> The Stars Above and the Root of All both played the Tremere for fools","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-26-2022, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T08:09:39-07:00","id":1481997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481983#post1481983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beckett's Jyhad Diary tied that Evil and Good Saulot thing up nicely, with Saulot P'o running amok and became the White Worm under Vienna while his Hun manifested as the &quot;Good Saulot&quot;<br /> This based on the tie with Kuei Jin, Saulot as Zao-Lat, a student of Xue, a thief, a despicable creature who benefited from Xue's compassion, learned Ch'iuh Muh - wich he not really udnerstanded and refined to be Valeren - then ran back home leaving behind his mess the Wu Zao and along the way made a Baali, when his P'o took control - or you know very Devil Tiger like behavior; the formation of the Baali may have been, in some incomprehensible way, a service for good in the long run. Clanbook: Baali suggests the Baali's ultimate purpose is the setting of chthonic entities (called Children) with sacrifice. Without these sacrifices, the Children would awaken and devour creation. Thus, the Baali's seeming evil protects humanity from a worse fate. Saulot may have sired the Baali to serve this purpose.<br /> More so, Kindred of the East allows you as a salubri player to actually awaken your P'o (beast) and start your Dharmic journey (players guide I think)!<br /> Then again, in V20 Goratrix during the Dark Ages was, in fact, Tremere, having been forced outside his body after he was possessed by Saulot<br /> Wich actually lines up nicely in Lair o the Hidden where Mokur (the Jomon potter golconda teacher from Japan) when was &quot;captured&quot; asked his captors to &quot;take him to his Father&quot;<br /> The Stars Above and the Root of All both played the Tremere for fools</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I havent got to the kindered of the east book yet, so I didnt know. Is the dynamic journey similar to the paths of enlightenment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T09:15:35-07:00","id":1482003,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Hello;n1481875]In the dark ages salubri clanbook, we learn that the salubri and tzimisce have a very close relationship. In fact it is stated that warriors and healers of clan salubri were able to learn more about their powers by watching the tzimisce torture their victims. So why is it that a clan that's supposed to be filled with paragons of justice are willing to consort with such sadistic monsters?<br /> <br /> Pragmatism. Just look at the real world and how we are willing to make deals with groups we detest if it serves our interests. As we been reminded time and time again, not everyone fits into a single box. you can have Salburi that are disgrace to the there clans ideals and Tzimisce who are not into mindless brutality and can be quite civil and reasonable.<br /> <br /> I guess that both antidulivans had a fairly close relationships in the ancient past and shared notes and I believe they even conversed with Cappadocious in completing their goals.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T10:58:00-07:00","id":1482010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1481875-the-salubri-who-are-known-as-the-good-guys-regularly-consorted-with-the-tzimisce?p=1481997#post1481997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I havent got to the kindered of the east book yet, so I didnt know. Is the dynamic journey similar to the paths of enlightenment?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit more... complicated<br /> For the Kuei-jin, a Dharma is a path to enlightenment which allows them to transcend their bestial natures and holds out hope for enlightenment and rejoining the Karmic cycle. As demonic creatures, enlightenment is far harder for Kuei-Jin, and the path to wisdom can take millennia.<br /> Dharmas are paths and &quot;clans&quot;, BUT you are not tied to a Dharma, its not uncomon for a Kuei-jin to &quot;try out&quot; several Dharmas before finding his calling<br /> The Kuei-jin advance in their Dharma by achieving moments of enlightenment, called dah. These moments arrive rarely, and can be triggered by great insight into one's dharma, or occasionally by great diversion from it. Each step of the way is progressively harder, with the time between moments of enlightenment taking years, then centuries, then millennia at the highest levels.<br /> Physically, higher enlightenment brings rewards. Dharmas traditionally follow a ten step path, with a chih-mei (a Kuei-jin that crawled back from Hell and yet to be civilized by a ritual by the others) having a rating of zero, and the Hundred Clouds (&quot;The Hundred Clouds&quot; is a metaphorical term for ultimate peace, the transcendent state in which even the duties of Heaven are set aside. The Clouds are not power, although lesser Kuei-jin might see them that way; they are not illusions, though they might seem so to individuals who cannot understand them. By joining The Hundred Clouds (which the wise understand to be a symbol, not a group), a Kuei-jin reaches the peak of its being, even higher than a bodhisattva. Most leave this world behind after reaching such heights, vanishing to an unknown destination. Others chose to remain and guide others as bodhisattvas.) at rank 10. In Kindred terms, a Kuei-Jin has a Generation roughly equivalent to 13 - their Dharma score. In particular, with a Dharma above 5, the Kuei Jin can raise their attributes to 6 or higher. In addition, Dharma rank influences how much chi can be stored and spent, and what type of nourishment a Kuei-Jin can take. Chih-mei subsist on flesh, low-dharma Kuei-Jin on blood (Dharma 1+), higher dharma Kuei-Jin on breath (Dharma 5+), and the most enlightened can absorb chi ambiently (Dharma 6+). Social role is determined at least partly by Dharma too<br /> Dharmas have a signture &quot;trait&quot; , a primary virtue<br /> <b>The Howl of the Devil-Tiger </b> (P'o - The P'o is an archetypal personality, serving the same function as a wraith's Shadow, or a Cainite's Beast. In addition, all Kuei-jin characters (and dhampyrs) have a P'o attribute, which governs the strength of the lower soul relative to the higher soul). - The Devil-Tigers believe that they are replacements for the incompetent demons of ages past; they punish sinners and seek enlightenment through pain and violence.<br /> <b>The Way of the Resplendent Crane </b>(Hun - The Hun is the higher, rational half of the soul. It is also akin to morality, conscience, honor and devotion to duty. The other half, animalistic and bestial is the P'o. The Hun score is used to resist control by the P'o.). - The Way of the Resplendent Crane is a highly legalistic collection of schools, dedicated to reversing the Wheel of Ages and restoring virtue.<br /> <b>The Song of the Shadow</b> (Yin - The Yin principle represents all that is passive, cold, dark, feminine, downward-seeking, and corresponds to the night. Of special interest to the Kuei-jin is the association of Yin with death and the dead. It is personified by the Ebon Dragon, and can be found in abundance in the Yin World.). - The yin-aspected Song of the Shadow, also known as Bone Flowers, are coldly logical necromancers who seek dispassionate reasoning and enforcement of dharmic balance. They are also tightly tied to mortal society through their descendants, and often assist their families even centuries afterward.<br /> <b>The Dance of the Thrashing Dragon</b> (Yang - Yang is one of the two forces which drive creation, along with Yin. The Yang principle represents all that is active, warm, bright, masculine, upward-seeking, and corresponds to the day. Of special interest to the Kuei-jin is the association of Yang with life and, by association, blood. It is personified by the Scarlet Queen/Scarlet Phoneix, and can be found in abundance in the Yang World.). - The often misunderstood Thrashing Dragon dharma recognizes that they are dead, but seeks to achieve enlightenment by imitating and interacting with the living. Despite the stunned disbelief of some Resplendent Cranes, they are a fully recognized Dharma, even if they seem to eat and screw their way through unlife.<br /> <b>The Path of a Thousand Whispers</b> (Balance - A Kuei-jin in attunement with Balance has his Yin and Yang Chi Virtues on an equal rating. In Kuei-jin society, they're the sages, the wanderers, and the seekers of truth. Of all Wan Kuei, they are the ones most interested in inner fulfillment and self-mastery. Vampires who strike for balance realize that they're neither entirely human nor entirely monstrous. They see the undead state as the first step in a riddle of sorts - just as the Buddha could seek enlightenment only when properly centered, so in damnation they have centered themselves between the fundamental poles of existence. Of all Wan Kuei, they are perhaps the most comfortable with what they have become, and yet, of all Hungry Dead, they most desire to transcend their state.). - The Thousand Whispers live a sequence of masks, new identities they construct after death in order to understand mortal life and hopefully transcend it. To follow the Whispering Way, a Kuei-jin must continually die and be reborn. Every few years, she suffers a ritual &quot;death,&quot; is buried, and returns as a new person. During her burial, the vampire enters a long trance, during which she meditates on the lessons of her past life. Certain powerful Whispers project their soul into the spirit worlds while the body sleeps. The Kuei-jin's body remains in stasis, guarded by mortal friends or other Whispers. The former are usually devoured when the vampire returns from her travels; the latter salute her and walk away as she emerges from the tomb. Each time she &quot;dies,&quot; the Kuei-jin severs all ties to her past life; in time, she walks away from her wu and court as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-26-2022, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T20:50:50-07:00","id":1482050,"title":"","content":"I always figure it was a dig at the &quot;evulz&quot; Tzimisce concept. In that, yes, the Tzimisce are more open about it and have a bit more shock value to their evil but they are not actually outliers in terms if evil done by the Cainites.The rest of the Clans are as bad even while many have a bit more PR work to make it look &quot;not as bad&quot;. Reminds me of a scene in popular book where one character remembers how some murdered bodies were wrapped in red cloaks to make the blood look less aweful as the bodies are presented.<br /> <br /> Some Cainites wrap their victims in a very nice red cloak. But they are just as dead all the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}